    "narrative": "The Austin Waves are primed for a high-ceiling outing today, headlined by **Kyle Tucker**, who commands an elite score of 78.68. Facing the vulnerable Randy V\u00e1squez (4.94 xERA), **Kyle Tucker** benefits from a massive SP-skill advantage that outweighs the modest park penalties. He is flanked by **Josh Jung** (66.30) and **Andy Pages** (65.90), both of whom capitalize on favorable matchups against suboptimal starting pitching. **Josh Jung** is particularly well-positioned, as his score reflects a significant 14% park boost, while **Andy Pages** leverages his high-contact profile against V\u00e1squez to maintain a strong 65.90 efficiency rating despite the risk of elite defensive positioning. \n\nStrategic lineup construction today heavily favors speed and matchup leverage, specifically with **Josh Lowe** and **Nasim Nunez** in the mix to bolster our scarcity-driven SB target. **Josh Lowe** (63.20) draws a dynamic platoon edge that pushes his utility well above the baseline, even with the lower-order batting position. On the bench, **Jackson Merrill** (49.38) presented the most difficult decision, coming close to a start but ultimately losing out due to an unfavorable clash with Shohei Ohtani. While **Jackson Merrill** holds latent talent, the 19% SP-skill drag created by Ohtani made him a clear sit compared to the stable efficiency of **Gage Workman** or **Dominic Smith**. We continue to monitor **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (57.28); while his score remains solid, the matchup against a 3.50 xERA arm demands caution, though his elite xwOBA keeps him locked into the UTIL spot over lower-ceiling options like **Liam Hicks**.",
